{"id":1826,"date":"2026-08-25T12:45:53","date_gmt":"2026-08-25T12:45:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/?post_type=knowledgebase&#038;p=1826"},"modified":"2026-08-25T17:29:52","modified_gmt":"2026-08-25T17:29:52","slug":"the-accessibility-checker","status":"publish","type":"knowledgebase","link":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/db\/accessibility\/the-accessibility-checker\/","title":{"rendered":"The Accessibility Checker"},"content":{"rendered":"<div style=\"color: #2b2b2b;\">\n<h2 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">The Accessibility Checker<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1840\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheAccessibilityChecker.webp\" alt=\"The Accessibility Checker\" width=\"153\" height=\"159\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheAccessibilityChecker.webp 924w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheAccessibilityChecker-289x300.webp 289w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/TheAccessibilityChecker-768x797.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 153px) 100vw, 153px\" \/><\/span><\/h2>\n<p class=\"western\">The Accessibility Checker scans your entire document for common accessibility violations and provides a dedicated task pane with one-click fixes, ensuring your publications are fully readable by screen readers and comply with <strong>WCAG 2.1<\/strong> guidelines.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Running the Accessibility Checker<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1830\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-25-134823.png\" alt=\"Accessibility Checker Button\" width=\"121\" height=\"128\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Go to the <strong>Review<\/strong> ribbon tab.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Click <strong>Accessibility Checker<\/strong>.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">The Accessibility task pane slides out on the right and scans across all pages.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">What It Checks<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1832\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/WhatTheAccessibilityCheckerChecks.webp\" alt=\"What It Checks\" width=\"133\" height=\"145\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">The checker flags three types of issue:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Missing Alt Text (High severity) \u2014<\/strong> Images without a descriptive alt attribute. Screen readers will be unable to describe these to visually impaired users.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Low Colour Contrast (High severity) \u2014<\/strong> Text and background colour combinations that do not meet WCAG 2.1 minimum contrast ratios.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Illogical Heading Structure (Medium severity) \u2014<\/strong> Detects missing H1 headings, skipped heading levels (for example, jumping from H1 directly to H3), and pages with no headings at all.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Fixing Issues<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1834\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/FixingIssuesWithTheAccessibilityChecker.webp\" alt=\"Fixing Issues\" width=\"144\" height=\"155\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/FixingIssuesWithTheAccessibilityChecker.webp 422w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/FixingIssuesWithTheAccessibilityChecker-279x300.webp 279w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 144px) 100vw, 144px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">For each flagged issue, the task pane shows a colour-coded severity indicator (red for high, orange for medium), a description of the problem, and a <strong>Fix Issue<\/strong> button that instantly navigates to the offending element and triggers the appropriate repair workflow \u2014 for example, opening the Alt Text dialog for a missing alt attribute, or applying a high-contrast theme for a contrast failure.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Auto-Fix Missing Titles<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1837\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/AutoFixMissingTitles.webp\" alt=\"Auto-Fix Missing Titles\" width=\"140\" height=\"147\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/AutoFixMissingTitles.webp 422w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/AutoFixMissingTitles-286x300.webp 286w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 140px) 100vw, 140px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">The scanner can automatically generate and insert an H1 page title on any page that is missing one, directly from the <strong>Fix Issue<\/strong> button \u2014 no manual editing required.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Accessibility Checker The Accessibility Checker scans your entire document for common accessibility violations and provides a dedicated task pane with one-click fixes, ensuring your publications are fully readable by screen readers and comply with WCAG 2.1 guidelines. Running the Accessibility Checker Go to the Review ribbon tab. Click Accessibility Checker. The Accessibility task pane [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1840,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","template":"","knowledgebase_cat":[23],"class_list":["post-1826","knowledgebase","type-knowledgebase","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","knowledgebase_cat-accessibility"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1826","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/knowledgebase"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1826"}],"version-history":[{"count":14,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1826\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1847,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1826\/revisions\/1847"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1840"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1826"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"knowledgebase_cat","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase_cat?post=1826"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}